  "body": "### Description\r\n\r\nhello, I found an event that is causing issues in Synapse.\r\n\r\nThe issue is that Synapse will raise an error when trying to decode the query result in `bg_updates.py` line `136`, I lost the stack from my logs but here is the error generated:\r\n`UnicodeDecodeError: 'utf-8' codec can't decode byte 0xf8 in position 21: invalid start byte`\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\n#### update:\r\n\r\nsee this comment below: https://github.com/matrix-org/synapse/issues/11921#issuecomment-1031092418\r\n\r\n#### or\r\n\r\nMaking a call to `_get_state_groups_from_groups` that target the room `!CCRKncVOQamqtSzFBm:matrix.org` should make it throw the error.\r\n\r\nCompressing the states of the room with https://github.com/matrix-org/rust-synapse-compress-state should make the appropriate call and fail.\r\n\r\nAttempting to delete the room will also fail because of this error.\r\n\r\nTo dig in the problem I did this:\r\n - call this API and save the result to a file: `https://matrix.homeserver.tld/_synapse/admin/v1/rooms/!CCRKncVOQamqtSzFBm:matrix.org/state?dir=b&from=0&order_by=id`\r\n\r\n- run this command to find the culprit characters: `grep --color='auto' -P -n \"[^\\x00-\\x7F]\" dump.json`\r\n\r\n### Version information\r\n\r\n- **Homeserver**:\r\n\r\nanother homeserver\r\n\r\n- **Version**:\r\n\r\n1.51\r\n\r\n- **Install method**:\r\n\r\nwe are using this playbook:\r\nhttps://github.com/spantaleev/matrix-docker-ansible-deploy\r\n\r\n- **Platform**:\r\n\r\ndeployed on Docker in Ubuntu LTS\r\n",
